```sql
--Description: We must first discover the exact spelling of the Speckled Tee
--             product so later joins/filters are accurate.  Because GA4 daily
--             export tables are named events_YYYYMMDD, use the wildcard
--             events_* and rely on BigQuery’s automatic `_TABLE_SUFFIX` to
--             limit the scan to December 2020 (20201201‑20201231).  The
--             `items` column is an ARRAY of STRUCTs, therefore `UNNEST(items)`
--             converts each product in a purchase into its own row.  Finally,
--             apply a case‑insensitive LIKE filter that matches both words
--             “speckled” and “tee”, then return the unique item names so we
--             know the precise label.
SELECT DISTINCT item.item_name
FROM  `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`
     ,UNNEST(items) AS item
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
  AND LOWER(item.item_name) LIKE '%speckled%tee%'
LIMIT 20;
```
